-- title:
--   Haar measure on local GL₂ is invariant under g↦ ^tg⁻¹
-- statement:
--   Let $v$ be a height-one prime of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $F = \mathbb{Q}_v$ be the associated adic completion. The group $GL_2(F)$ is equipped with the measurable structure `localGLBorel ℚ v`, namely the Borel $\sigma$-algebra generated by its topology, together with the corresponding `BorelSpace` instance. The assertion is that for every measure $\mu_2$ on $GL_2(F)$ which is a Haar measure (in Mathlib's sense: left invariant, regular, finite on compact sets and positive on nonempty open sets), the push-forward of $\mu_2$ along the map $h \mapsto$ `transposeInvN (Fin 2) h` equals $\mu_2$. Here `transposeInvN (Fin 2) h` denotes the element of $GL_2(F)$ whose underlying matrix is the transpose of the matrix of $h^{-1}$ and whose inverse is the transpose of the matrix of $h$; that is, the involution $h \mapsto {}^t h^{-1}$. Thus $\mu_2$ is invariant under transpose-inverse.
--
--   The statement records that the transpose-inverse involution of $GL_2$ over a nonarchimedean local field preserves Haar measure, so that the substitution $h \mapsto {}^t h^{-1}$ (and its composites with Weyl elements) may be performed freely inside local integrals. It is used in the local Rankin–Selberg computations, in particular in the treatment of Godement–Whittaker integrals, of zeta integrals attached to principal series, and of their functional equations.
